To implement the PDF to Text Converter API using the Lumen framework, we will follow the OpenAPI schema provided and ensure that the application is set up correctly. Below is the complete implementation:

### File Structure and Code

#### 1. `.env`

<FILEPATH>
.env
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
APP_NAME=Lumen
APP_ENV=local
APP_KEY=
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_URL=http://localhost

LOG_CHANNEL=stack

DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
DB_DATABASE=/app/db.sqlite3
</CODE>

#### 2. `bootstrap/app.php`

<FILEPATH>
bootstrap/app.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

require_once __DIR__.'/../vendor/autoload.php';

$app = new Laravel\Lumen\Application(
    dirname(__DIR__)
);

$app->withFacades();
$app->withEloquent();

$app->register(App\Providers\AppServiceProvider::class);

$app->router->group([
    'namespace' => 'App\Http\Controllers',
], function ($router) {
    require __DIR__.'/../routes/web.php';
});

return $app;
</CODE>

#### 3. `routes/web.php`

<FILEPATH>
routes/web.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

/** @var \Laravel\Lumen\Routing\Router $router */

$router->post('/convert', 'PDFController@convert');
</CODE>

#### 4. `app/Http/Controllers/PDFController.php`

<FILEPATH>
app/Http/Controllers/PDFController.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;

class PDFController extends Controller
{
    public function convert(Request $request)
    {
        if (!$request->hasFile('file') || !$request->file('file')->isValid()) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Invalid input or missing file'], Response::HTTP_BAD_REQUEST);
        }

        $file = $request->file('file');
        $filePath = $file->getPathname();
        $outputPath = tempnam(sys_get_temp_dir(), 'txt');

        try {
            $command = sprintf('pdftotext %s %s', escapeshellarg($filePath), escapeshellarg($outputPath));
            exec($command, $output, $returnVar);

            if ($returnVar !== 0) {
                throw new \Exception('Conversion failed');
            }

            $text = file_get_contents($outputPath);
            unlink($outputPath);

            return response($text, Response::HTTP_OK)->header('Content-Type', 'text/plain');
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Internal Server Error - Conversion failed'], Response::HTTP_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
        }
    }
}
</CODE>

#### 5. `app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`

<FILEPATH>
app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Providers;

use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

class AppServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register()
    {
        //
    }

    public function boot()
    {
        //
    }
}
</CODE>

### Running the Application

To start the application, use the following command:

```bash
php -S 0.0.0.0:5000 -t public
```

This will start the Lumen application on port `5000`, and you can access the API endpoint at `http://localhost:5000/convert`.

### Testing the API

You can test the API using a tool like `curl` or Postman by sending a POST request to the `/convert` endpoint with a PDF file as form-data under the key `file`. The API will return the extracted text from the PDF file.

This implementation ensures that the application is set up correctly and follows the OpenAPI schema provided. The use of `pdftotext` for conversion is handled securely with `escapeshellarg` to prevent command injection vulnerabilities.

